# Marketing demo videos are stored in Git LFS, but these patterns deliberately
# omit `filter=lfs` — only diff/merge are set. That keeps git-lfs OPTIONAL:
# contributors who don't need the videos can clone without it and get ~130-byte
# pointer files. Do NOT add `filter=lfs` here — it would make git-lfs mandatory
# for every clone, which is exactly what this setup avoids.
#
# The trade-off: with no clean filter, nothing converts real bytes back into a
# pointer, so once you have the real media every one of these files is "modified"
# forever. Most are masked by git's stat cache and never show in `git status`,
# which makes `git add -A` / `git commit -a` genuinely dangerous here — they can
# bake tens of MB of binaries into history and destroy the pointers. Stage
# release and version files explicitly instead.
#
# Marketing contributors — to get the real videos AND keep `git status` clean:
#
#   brew install git-lfs && git lfs install   # hooks; does not fix the above
#   git lfs fetch --all                       # downloads objects to .git/lfs/objects
#
#   # NOTE: `git lfs pull` and `git lfs checkout` do NOT populate the working
#   # tree in this repo — both rely on the smudge filter these patterns omit.
#   # Copy the bytes out of the local LFS cache instead (oid + path come from
#   # `git lfs ls-files -l`):
#   #     cp .git/lfs/objects/<ab>/<cd>/<oid>  <path>
#
#   # Then tell git to stop comparing them. skip-worktree is local index state,
#   # never pushed, so it changes nothing for anyone else:
#   git lfs ls-files -n | tr '\n' '\0' | xargs -0 git update-index --skip-worktree
#
# Verify with `git ls-files -v packages/marketing/public/videos/` (expect mostly
# `S`). Undo with `--no-skip-worktree` — required if upstream ever changes one of
# these files, since git refuses to overwrite a skip-worktree entry on pull.
packages/marketing/public/videos/*.mp4 diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
packages/marketing/public/videos/*.webm diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
packages/marketing/public/videos/posters/*.jpg diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
